//! evaluator/types/utils — type-system utility helpers.
//!
//! TS counterpart: `src/evaluator/types/utils.ts` (~2000 lines).
//!
//! Status: stub. The TS file aggregates several distinct concerns:
//!
//!   1. Self-type module composition: `addFunctionSignatureToSelfTypeModule`,
//!      `addFunctionCodeToSelfTypeModule`. Signature constants for `dispose`,
//!      `___drop`, `___dup`.
//!   2. RC machinery installation: `addRcFunctionsTo{Struct,Enum,Dyn,Some,Iso}Type`
//!      and the matching `addRcFunctionSignaturesTo{Struct,Enum}Type` helpers.
//!   3. Trait attachment: `attachTraitToReceiverType`.
//!   4. Auto-derive logic: `autoDerive{Send,Rc,Acyclic,Comptime,Runtime}For{Struct,Enum,Union,Tuple}Type`
//!      and the orchestrators `autoDeriveTraitsAndAddRcFunctionsFor{Struct,Enum}Type`.
//!
//! In yo-self these concerns are currently split:
//!
//!   - The auto-derive portion lives in `yo-self/evaluator/types/auto_derive.yo`.
//!   - Send/Rc/Acyclic trait-check helpers live in
//!     `yo-self/evaluator/trait_checking.yo`.
//!   - RC signature installation is currently scattered (or stubbed) across
//!     `evaluator/types/{struct,enum,union,object,dyn,iso}.yo`.
//!
//! Migration plan (follow-up port):
//!   - Merge `types/auto_derive.yo` content here under matching function names.
//!   - Pull the RC-signature helpers out of their per-type files into this
//!     module so each TS function has a 1:1 yo counterpart.
//!   - Keep `evaluator/trait_checking.yo` as-is (its TS home is
//!     `src/evaluator/trait-checking.ts`, a separate file).
//!
//! This stub exists so the evaluator/types/ directory mirrors the TS tree
//! 1-to-1.
